cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below. For the (72,108) exclusion itself, please cite Helali (2026) — see `references` — who published it first."
title: "The plane (72,108) Jacobian case — an independent structural proof"
abstract: >-
  An independent structural proof that both Newton-polygon configurations of the
  GGV-Horruitiner (8,28)/(72,108) case (arXiv:2204.14178, Prop 4.3) are empty,
  so that — conditional on that proposition being exhaustive and on the
  alpha-strip WLOG — any plane Jacobian-Conjecture counterexample has
  max(deg P, deg Q) >= 125. Priority for the exclusion belongs to B. Helali,
  who published an independent treatment on 2026-07-21; this work is a second,
  structurally different route whose intermediate content is finer than a
  yes/no answer, including the exact valuation pin a_t = 9 and a five-case
  classification of admissible germs. Also includes an independent exact
  re-verification of the dimension-3 Jacobian counterexample. Every claim is
  catalogued with its checker and a trust tier, and none of the proof's eleven
  machine steps is irreducibly machine work.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Strinz"
    given-names: "Will"
keywords:
  - "Jacobian Conjecture"
  - "polynomial automorphisms"
  - "computer-assisted proof"
  - "Newton polygon"
  - "valuation"
license: MIT
